---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MemoHeader from '../components/MemoHeader.astro';
import SignatureBlock from '../components/SignatureBlock.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why dumbGTM exists: a marketing idea that got me fired, then worked somewhere else.">
  <article class="container-memo pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <div class="max-w-[68ch] flex flex-col gap-7">
      <MemoHeader rows={[
        { label: 'TO:', value: 'Whoever asked' },
        { label: 'FROM:', value: 'The Author' },
        { label: 'RE:', value: 'The origin story' },
      ]} />
      <h1 class="t-h1 text-ink">Why "dumb"?</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-memo mt-10">
      <p>
        A while back I pitched a marketing idea at work. It was cheap, a bit odd, and nobody in
        our space was doing it. Leadership thought it was a dumb idea. Not long after that, I was
        let go.
      </p>
      <p>At my next job I pitched the same idea, and my new boss told me to try it. It worked.</p>
      <p>The idea was the same at both companies. What changed was whether someone let me try it.</p>
      <p>
        Since then I've noticed the same pattern all over marketing. The tactics everyone uses now
        started out as ideas someone had to fight for. Then they worked, everyone copied them, and
        they got boring. Then someone came up with a new dumb idea and the loop started again.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <p>
        Blog posts and videos about marketing ideas that sound wrong at first. Some of them are
        early. Some are old ideas that have gone stale and need retiring. A few will be bad, and
        I'll say so when that happens.
      </p>

      <h2>Who's writing this</h2>
      <p>
        I've worked in growth and lifecycle marketing for most of my career. For now I'm keeping my
        name off the site. Judge the ideas, not the byline.
      </p>

      <h2>Say hi</h2>
      <p>Got a dumb idea your team shot down? <a href="/contact">Send it over.</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-[68ch] mt-10">
      <SignatureBlock name="The Author" subtitle="Name withheld. Feelings: on file." />
      <div class="double-rule mt-12"></div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
